    "created_at": "2016-02-23T17:56:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-23T17:56:02Z",
    "body": "Yeah, we could change the normative text too to be clearer here. Note that it varies based on the user agent whether it's actually represented as a text control. I think Chrome does that, but mobile Safari definitely doesn't. Perhaps if we change the normative language to \"if the control has no interactive text field\" it's a little clearer?\n\nWe might have to update the text for certain other methods/attributes too then, though.\n",
